<article class="env-lemma" id="0792">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0792">Lemma <span data-tag="0792">7.45.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $a, b : V \to U$ be objects of $\mathcal{C}$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ h_ V^\#  \ar@<1ex>[r] \ar@<-1ex>[r] &  h_ U^\#  \ar[r] &  {*} }  \]
</div>
  <p> is a coequalizer in $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. Then $\Gamma (\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{F})$ is the equalizer of $a^*, b^* : \mathcal{F}(U) \to \mathcal{F}(V)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $\mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})}(h_ U^\# , \mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{F}(U)$ this is clear from the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>